y\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids in Lebanon County has 75 years on record, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 36 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle saw May to June at 191% of normal and August to September at 47%. So far in 2026, May to June sits at 59% of normal on the middle. Grid 24215 had its driest year in 1965 at 67%.</p>"}
